## 2. Applicant Flow — Delayed Login (No Account on Apply)

### New Application Flow

```
PUBLIC (no login required):
════════════════════════════
Step 0: Screening Questions (knockout check)
  │  
  │  ALL answers stored regardless of qualification
  │  Silently flagged if fails requirements
  │  
Step 1: Personal Details (name, email, phone)
  │  NO password field — no account created
  │  
Step 2: Professional Background
  │  Work experience, sales background
  │  
Step 3: Resume Upload
  │  Upload via server-side API (no auth needed)
  │  
Step 4: Terms & Privacy Agreement
  │  Checkboxes + timestamp
  │  
  ✅ "Application Received" confirmation page
     (They get a confirmation email via Resend)
     (They get a tracking code: e.g. "ONX-2026-0042")

LATER (HR decides to advance them):
════════════════════════════════════
HR reviews application → clicks "Approve & Send Account Invite"
  │
  │  System sends magic link email to applicant
  │  Applicant clicks link → creates password → account active
  │  
  ✅ Now they can log in to:
     ├── /dashboard — See their application status
     ├── /exam — Take assigned exams
     ├── /dashboard/contract — Sign e-contract (if hired)
     └── /dashboard/training — Access training (if agent)
```

### Database Change
Since applicants no longer have a Supabase auth account at application time, we need a separate table:

```sql
-- Stores applications BEFORE they have an auth account
CREATE TABLE public.applications (
  id uuid default gen_random_uuid() primary key,
  tracking_code text unique not null,     -- "ONX-2026-0042"
  
  -- Personal Details
  first_name text not null,
  last_name text not null,
  email text not null,
  phone text,
  
  -- Professional Background
  work_experience text,
  sales_background text,
  
  -- Resume
  resume_url text,
  
  -- Screening
  screening_responses jsonb,              -- { question_id: answer, ... }
  screening_qualified boolean,            -- auto-computed
  screening_flags jsonb,                  -- reasons for disqualification
  
  -- Job
  applied_position_id uuid references job_positions(id),
  
  -- Legal Consent
  terms_accepted_at timestamptz,
  privacy_accepted_at timestamptz,
  
  -- Pipeline
  stage text default 'New' check (stage in (
    'New',                    -- just submitted
    'Screening Review',       -- screener is reviewing
    'Qualified',              -- passed screening
    'Disqualified',           -- failed screening (HR decided)
    'Account Invited',        -- magic link sent
    'Exam Assigned',          -- exam is ready for them
    'Exam Completed',         -- they finished the exam
    'Interview Scheduled',
    'Interview Completed', 
    'Offer Extended',
    'Contract Sent',
    'Contract Signed',
    'Hired',
    'Rejected',
    'Withdrawn'
  )),
  
  -- Link to auth account (NULL until they create one)
  user_id uuid references auth.users(id),
  
  -- Notes
  internal_notes text,
  
  -- Timestamps
  created_at timestamptz default now(),
  updated_at timestamptz default now()
);
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This `applications` table replaces the old approach of writing directly to `profiles`. It solves the "one job limit" bug AND supports the delayed login flow. One person can submit multiple applications to different positions.

### Tracking Code System
- Format: `ONX-{YEAR}-{4-DIGIT-SEQUENTIAL}` (e.g., `ONX-2026-0042`)
- Applicant receives this in their confirmation email
- Public page `/track` — enter email or tracking code to see status (without login)

